# Patch:     060-qualify-internal-layer-mat-mul
# Phase:     post-extraction
# Target:    extraction/p3_baby_bear.lean
# Hunks:     1
# Cost:      none
# Upstream:  hax bug -- a hoisted helper is referenced unqualified from inside an
#            instance that has a field of the same name, so the reference
#            resolves to the instance's own projection.
# Drop when: hax fully qualifies references to helpers it hoists.
#
# hax hoists `internal_layer_mat_mul` out of the Poseidon2 instance into
# `Impl_2.internal_layer_mat_mul_hoisted`, then refers to it unqualified from
# within the instance of the same name. Name resolution prefers the enclosing
# instance's projection, producing a self-reference that does not elaborate.
#
# The patch spells the intended target in full
# (`p3_baby_bear.poseidon2.Impl_2.internal_layer_mat_mul_hoisted`). The original
# is preserved as a comment. No definition changes -- only which of two
# same-named things the reference points at.
#
--- a/extraction/p3_baby_bear.lean
+++ b/extraction/p3_baby_bear.lean
@@ -4207,7 +4207,8 @@
         R]
       [trait_constr__i0 : p3_field.field.PrimeCharacteristicRing R ]
